{
  "biological_interpretation": "The ankyrin-G intracellular scaffold maintains a thalamic synaptic/calcium transcriptional state that is not a generic readout of paranodal adhesion or spectrin loss.",
  "caveats": [
    "The link from Ank3 RNA loss to axon-initial-segment biology is inferred from known protein function; AIS integrity was not measured.",
    "Ank1 and Ank2 were weakly engaged, while the Cntn1/Cntnap1/Sptan1 negative comparators were much stronger."
  ],
  "cell_types": [
    "151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut"
  ],
  "exact_observed_result": "Ank3 perturbation in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut produced 121 FDR<0.05 genes, including reductions of Opn3, Atp2a2, Atp2b1, Erc2, Vgf, Ache, Cacna2d1, Gabra4, Grm1, and Gria4 and induction of Pcsk1n, while Ank1, Cntn1, Cntnap1, and Sptan1 failed to reproduce the state.",
